WEBVTT

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:13.208
Now, then, Koro Sensei.
Let your final death match begin.

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:16.000
Koro Sensei...

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.333
Compared to me, you are...

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:19.625
weak.

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:35.875
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:38.708
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:44.125
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:46.792
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:00:46.792 --> 00:00:49.500
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.292
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:57.292
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:00.250
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:05.458
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:11.083
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:16.500
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.000
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.625
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:27.292
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:01:27.292 --> 00:01:30.083
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.667
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.375
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:38.083
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.917
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:45.875
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:53.708
"Third Period: Itona Horibe Time"
"by Itona Horibe"

00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:57.875
Itona!

00:01:57.875 --> 00:02:01.958
First we make drastic changes to the field.

00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:04.125
--Ow ow ow!
--Then we attack.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:09.000
Easier to confine him first, then strike.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.750
I've taken a page from your tactics, you see.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.875
Shiro! So you were behind all this?

00:02:15.875 --> 00:02:17.250
Exactly.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.792
Once that creature
starts losing his students' trust,

00:02:19.792 --> 00:02:22.333
his movements grow panicked.

00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:25.542
Even if things seem a little
off somehow, he'll dive right in,

00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:27.500
the fool.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.292
Dammit! That's <i>our </i>kill!

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:33.417
Why do you always play so dirty?

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:37.125
It's called "being an adult."

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:40.083
What Itona has on his tentacles there

00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:43.667
are gloves with sharp edges
made of anti-Sensei materials.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.917
Every time their tentacles touch,
the creature's bare tentacles

00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:50.000
will continue to take damage.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.375
Seems that's not enough
to finish him off, though.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.625
I won, big brother.

00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:00.083
By killing you,

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:04.208
I'm solving just one problem:

00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:08.500
I'm proving... my strength!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.292
Yes, very well done, Itona!

00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:20.917
If this were before the first term,
you may very well have killed me.

00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:24.792
But your attack pattern is a simple one.

00:03:24.792 --> 00:03:27.250
No matter how fast you are,
no matter how strong,

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.625
no matter how many schemes
your guardian thinks up,

00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.792
no matter how easily I freak out,

00:03:31.792 --> 00:03:36.875
by our third fight, I can see
and adapt to your patterns.

00:03:36.875 --> 00:03:40.000
No way... it can't be...

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.333
Itona...

00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.875
I study, too, you know.

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:54.333
How could I teach anyone if
I didn't grow and learn day by day?

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:58.417
Now, let's get rid of
this dangerous cloth cage.

00:03:58.417 --> 00:04:01.375
Experiencing my Absolute Defense Form
over summer vacation

00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:04.125
taught me yet another skill:

00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:07.208
compressing not my whole body,
but a portion of my tentacles

00:04:07.208 --> 00:04:10.000
to release a burst of energy.

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:12.792
Wh-What...?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.167
Remember this, Itona.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.583
I say assassination <i>is </i>education.

00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:20.583
The assassination classroom's teacher

00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:23.583
will get stronger every time he teaches!

00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:31.250
Why... can't I... win?

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:37.208
I'm supposed to be... stronger now...

00:04:43.042 --> 00:04:45.958
So there you have it, Shiro.

00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:49.833
Leave him to the E Class and go quietly.

00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:51.167
Oh, and...

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.875
...spread the <i>accurate </i>word
that I am <i>not </i>an underwear thief!

00:04:54.875 --> 00:04:59.167
And I'm actually a B-cup! A B-cup!

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.167
I-It hurts...

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.292
--Itona!
--My head's... killing me!

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:14.417
My brain's about to burst!

00:05:14.417 --> 00:05:16.375
With the shock of his repeated defeats,

00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:18.833
his tentacles are starting
to gnaw away at his mind...

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:21.417
Hang in there, Itona!

00:05:21.417 --> 00:05:24.750
This might just be all he can take.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.792
Why, he can't even pull off
this little scheme of mine.

00:05:28.792 --> 00:05:30.958
Wh-What is he saying?

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:32.458
Itona,

00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:37.458
if this is all you're capable of,
the Organization will stop paying.

00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:39.708
It's not that I don't feel for you,

00:05:39.708 --> 00:05:42.208
but we have to cut our losses at some point

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.042
if only to get the next model up and running.

00:05:45.042 --> 00:05:50.250
This is goodbye, Itona.
You're on your own now.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.542
Wait! What kind of guardian are you, anyway?

00:05:53.542 --> 00:05:56.917
Quit playing school, you monster.

00:05:56.917 --> 00:06:01.250
All you can do is
break things--break everything.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:05.542
I will not countenance your existence.

00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:07.750
I wish only for your death...

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:11.542
no matter what the sacrifice.

00:06:12.583 --> 00:06:18.125
Say, are you sure your
dear students are okay like that?

00:06:19.708 --> 00:06:21.333
Look out!

00:06:28.917 --> 00:06:31.292
Itona...

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:36.042
Koro Sensei!

00:06:37.917 --> 00:06:42.042
As you might imagine,
I'm pooped. Time for a little rest.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.708
With tentacle cells
grafted to your human body,

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:53.000
you must undergo
adaptive treatment almost daily

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.333
or be tormented by hellish rejection symptoms.

00:06:57.333 --> 00:07:00.083
Now that I've stopped your maintenance,

00:07:00.083 --> 00:07:04.250
your tentacles will ultimately,
painfully eat away your nerves...

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:08.125
The average person
dies of madness in three days.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.208
Here's where the first incident occurred.

00:07:14.208 --> 00:07:19.792
A string of attacks on
cell phone shops throughout Kunugigaoka

00:07:19.792 --> 00:07:23.125
has the police discussing
a potential terrorism link.

00:07:23.125 --> 00:07:24.542
This has got to be...

00:07:24.542 --> 00:07:26.167
It's him, all right.

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:28.333
But why cell phone shops?

00:07:28.333 --> 00:07:30.042
What should we do, sir?

00:07:30.042 --> 00:07:33.458
As his teacher,
I'll take responsibility and stop him.

00:07:33.458 --> 00:07:36.292
I have to find him, protect him!

00:07:36.292 --> 00:07:39.458
I've got a good handle on Shiro's personality.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:43.792
To him, everyone's a pawn
to use and throw away--

00:07:43.792 --> 00:07:47.625
and you don't quite know
what a guy like that will do next.

00:07:47.625 --> 00:07:51.500
I think it'd be wiser to leave him alone.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.417
Even so, I'm his teacher.

00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:59.250
Don't let go of your students, no matter what.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:03.625
When I became a teacher, that was my vow.

00:08:12.375 --> 00:08:15.500
There are no shortcuts, Itona.

00:08:16.583 --> 00:08:21.458
Only those who study daily
and work with integrity

00:08:21.458 --> 00:08:23.667
will grow stronger.

00:08:24.917 --> 00:08:26.833
That liar.

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:32.917
"Mashimoto Imports"

00:08:40.833 --> 00:08:44.625
Forget lip service. No beating around the bush.

00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:49.667
Being a sore loser
makes me sick. I want to win.

00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:52.000
I want the strength to be able to win.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:57.417
Your human face is showing at last, Itona.

00:08:57.417 --> 00:08:58.667
Big brother...

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:01.458
"Koro Sensei," if you please.

00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:03.792
After all, I'm your teacher.

00:09:03.792 --> 00:09:07.042
Don't be goin' nuclear on us, now, Itona.

00:09:07.042 --> 00:09:10.542
You put us through a lotta stuff,
but we'll let it slide.

00:09:10.542 --> 00:09:12.750
Just come with us quietly.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:18.750
Shut up! We battle. This time... I'll win.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.083
Of course we can battle.

00:09:21.083 --> 00:09:25.708
Maybe we two state secrets
can find a vacant lot somewhere.

00:09:25.708 --> 00:09:28.917
Afterwards, we'll all study ways to kill me

00:09:28.917 --> 00:09:33.167
while we enjoy a little barbecue together.

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:35.208
He's a persistent one, that octopus.

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:40.125
Once he takes over, he'll go
to the depths of hell to teach you.

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:44.625
Of course! Put a student in front of me,

00:09:44.625 --> 00:09:48.542
and my instinct is to want to teach him or her.

00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:54.125
What <i>is </i>this?

00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:55.458
I can't see!

00:09:55.458 --> 00:09:59.333
Is this... anti-me powder?!

00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:04.125
Setting Itona adrift was
all part of the plan, Koro Sensei.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.958
I was so distracted by
Itona's bloodlust that I didn't notice!

00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:14.042
Come now, Itona--your final duty.

00:10:14.042 --> 00:10:15.917
Itona!

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.833
You'll come after him, won't you?
Being his teacher and all.

00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:29.958
Koro Sensei...

00:10:29.958 --> 00:10:33.125
Is everyone all right?

00:10:33.125 --> 00:10:34.542
More or less...

00:10:34.542 --> 00:10:39.167
Then I'll go rescue Itona!

00:10:39.167 --> 00:10:42.625
Protecting us reduced
his evasion response time.

00:10:42.625 --> 00:10:43.958
No!

00:10:43.958 --> 00:10:48.833
Damn that Shiro!
He made us his pawns, all right!

00:10:51.667 --> 00:10:55.708
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Karma Akabane"

00:11:00.833 --> 00:11:02.667
Itona!

00:11:04.708 --> 00:11:08.042
Pressure rays--to slow me down!

00:11:08.042 --> 00:11:12.500
Not that I'm surprised,
but you really are a fool, Koro Sensei.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.667
I'm after Itona.

00:11:17.542 --> 00:11:22.958
That's right: you grow weak
when the target is anyone but you.

00:11:22.958 --> 00:11:24.667
Now will you run away?

00:11:24.667 --> 00:11:26.792
I am his <i>teacher</i>!

00:11:26.792 --> 00:11:28.458
I...

00:11:28.458 --> 00:11:30.000
I'm powerless.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.333
That's why even my partner's abandoned me.

00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:40.333
Good eyes.

00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:44.000
In them I see a dogged fixation on winning--

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:50.292
crucial for making the most
of the powerful cells I've created.

00:11:50.292 --> 00:11:53.083
Why don't we do a little addition, you and me?

00:11:53.083 --> 00:11:56.958
Let me handle the path to victory.

00:11:56.958 --> 00:12:03.708
Your tenacity plus my tech
equals the power to seize victory.

00:12:03.708 --> 00:12:08.000
With power, you can be stronger
than anyone else in this world.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.417
I was dead set on power,

00:12:10.417 --> 00:12:13.708
so I could withstand the
searing pain of those mysterious cells.

00:12:13.708 --> 00:12:15.792
I was dead set on winning,

00:12:15.792 --> 00:12:18.250
so I could throw myself into it,
again and again.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:21.167
But I didn't get what I was after.

00:12:21.167 --> 00:12:24.042
And the one I was
meant to kill is protecting me!

00:12:24.042 --> 00:12:28.250
I... I can't lose to those nobodies...

00:12:31.833 --> 00:12:33.250
What the--

00:12:36.417 --> 00:12:39.083
This is anti-octopus cloth, right?

00:12:39.083 --> 00:12:44.333
That's why <i>we've </i>gotta take
you down instead of that octopus!

00:12:44.333 --> 00:12:47.500
Terasaka! Get the light in the tree!

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.792
On it!

00:12:48.792 --> 00:12:50.375
You brats...!

00:12:53.625 --> 00:12:55.958
But... why would you...

00:12:55.958 --> 00:12:58.125
Don't take this the wrong way.

00:12:58.125 --> 00:13:01.000
We're just ticked off at Shiro.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:04.833
If Koro Sensei hadn't run off,
we would have left you behind.

00:13:04.833 --> 00:13:07.542
Hayami said "Don't take this the wrong way!"

00:13:07.542 --> 00:13:10.917
Talk about running hot and cold!

00:13:10.917 --> 00:13:13.917
You sure you want to
be looking this way, Shiro?

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:19.708
If you stop shooting,
the netting'll come right off at the base.

00:13:19.708 --> 00:13:22.667
You made it!

00:13:22.667 --> 00:13:24.500
The netting is melting his tentacles!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.417
We'll get you out of there!

00:13:26.417 --> 00:13:28.292
Step down, Shiro.

00:13:28.292 --> 00:13:30.917
We'll take Itona.

00:13:30.917 --> 00:13:33.917
You always plan so carefully,

00:13:33.917 --> 00:13:37.917
but once my students get involved,
those plans are ruined.

00:13:37.917 --> 00:13:41.583
The sooner you notice the obvious, the better.

00:13:42.792 --> 00:13:46.125
A class consisting of a monster
swarmed by tiny flies?

00:13:46.125 --> 00:13:49.042
How infinitely irritating.

00:13:49.042 --> 00:13:55.125
But I will allow that my plan
needs some radical revisions.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:01.000
Keep the boy. He'll only live
another two, three days as it is.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.292
Play nice together, now.

00:14:05.583 --> 00:14:08.708
Studying, integrity--lies, all of it.

00:14:08.708 --> 00:14:14.042
In the end, it all comes down to
whether I have overwhelming strength.

00:14:16.083 --> 00:14:20.083
As long as Itona has a pathological
attachment to power and winning,

00:14:20.083 --> 00:14:23.292
his tentacle cells will stick so tight
that we can't remove them.

00:14:23.292 --> 00:14:25.500
Can't we cut them off somehow?

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.958
Not until we get rid of his attachment.

00:14:27.958 --> 00:14:31.667
That's why we have to know
more about how he got this way.

00:14:31.667 --> 00:14:33.167
Yeah, but...

00:14:33.167 --> 00:14:36.625
I kinda doubt he'll be
forthcoming about his life story.

00:14:36.625 --> 00:14:39.333
Actually, about that...

00:14:39.333 --> 00:14:41.042
I was curious:

00:14:41.042 --> 00:14:44.292
Why was Itona going after cell phone shops?

00:14:44.292 --> 00:14:44.500
"City Pages"
Why was Itona going after cell phone shops?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:48.625
"City Pages"
So I had Ritsu look up some stuff about him,

00:14:48.625 --> 00:14:49.250
"City Pages"
and it turns out

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:49.750
and it turns out

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.542
the president of this company

00:14:51.542 --> 00:14:51.708
had a son named Itona Horibe.

00:14:51.708 --> 00:14:53.333
"Horibe Electronics"
had a son named Itona Horibe.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:58.250
This little factory supplied
smartphone parts around the world.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:01.250
Two years ago it went under,
burdened with debt.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:04.958
The president and his wife vanished,
leaving their son behind.

00:15:04.958 --> 00:15:12.125
We started to see the reason behind
Itona's lust for power, for victory.

00:15:12.125 --> 00:15:17.583
Pfft, is that all?
That made him into a delinquent?

00:15:18.583 --> 00:15:21.125
Everybody's worried about somethin'.

00:15:21.125 --> 00:15:23.875
Big problems, little ones...

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:32.000
We'll take him in, look after him.
If he dies, well, that's that.

00:15:33.875 --> 00:15:37.708
Look, Itona. Even a tiny factory like ours

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:44.042
can compete with the big names
if we work with integrity.

00:15:44.042 --> 00:15:47.833
What a load of crap.

00:15:47.833 --> 00:15:53.250
But why? You know
all our techniques! If you leave us...

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:56.000
Studying and integrity are meaningless

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:00.167
in the face of superior, overwhelming power.

00:16:01.375 --> 00:16:06.083
I'm sorry, Itona. Go live with your uncle.

00:16:10.417 --> 00:16:13.042
You're awake. Finally.

00:16:14.958 --> 00:16:17.625
We refashioned the
anti-tentacle netting into a bandana.

00:16:17.625 --> 00:16:19.250
Just for peace of mind.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.542
But you can't pop out any tentacles, can you?

00:16:21.542 --> 00:16:23.500
"Ramen" "Gyoza" "Matsuraikan"

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.958
"Fried Rice" "Cold Tofu"
"Edamame" "Salt Ramen"

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:26.208
"Salt Ramen" "Miso Ramen" "Soy-Sauce Ramen"

00:16:26.208 --> 00:16:28.375
"Salt Ramen" "Miso Ramen" "Soy-Sauce Ramen"
Why ramen?

00:16:28.375 --> 00:16:33.000
"Salt Ramen" "Miso Ramen" "Soy-Sauce Ramen"
He's got to be hungry, right? He'll feel better after he eats.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:33.958
He's got to be hungry, right? He'll feel better after he eats.

00:16:33.958 --> 00:16:37.042
Well? Isn't our ramen totally gross?

00:16:37.042 --> 00:16:40.208
I keep telling my old man,
but he won't change the recipe.

00:16:40.208 --> 00:16:42.958
It <i>is </i>gross. And stale.

00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:46.083
The soup uses MSG to cover up
the corners cut on chicken bones.

00:16:46.083 --> 00:16:49.917
The main topping is a swirl
of fishcake, placed with pride.

00:16:49.917 --> 00:16:52.583
This is from four generations back.
This is 1950s ramen.

00:16:52.583 --> 00:16:54.875
This punk knows his stuff!

00:16:54.875 --> 00:16:59.083
If a chain store opened nearby,
this place would be toast.

00:16:59.083 --> 00:17:04.500
My father may have studied,
but he still suffered a tragic loss.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.917
Let's hit my place next.

00:17:06.917 --> 00:17:10.958
Our modern tech'll put
this fossilized ramen to shame!

00:17:10.958 --> 00:17:12.042
Why, you--!

00:17:12.042 --> 00:17:14.583
"Yoshida Motors"

00:17:16.292 --> 00:17:19.833
Whaddya think, Itona?
Let the speed blow your cares away!

00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:22.083
An unlicensed junior-high kid?
You sure about this?

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:24.333
It <i>is </i>on Yoshida's family property.

00:17:24.333 --> 00:17:26.667
Feeling good and hyped?

00:17:26.667 --> 00:17:27.833
It's not bad.

00:17:27.833 --> 00:17:31.667
All riiight!
Now for my high-speed braking turn!

00:17:33.625 --> 00:17:38.083
You idiot! Go help him!
What if the shock sets him off again?!

00:17:38.083 --> 00:17:40.750
Aw, that's not enough to hurt him!

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:43.167
They're just flying by the seat of their pants.

00:17:43.167 --> 00:17:44.875
Yeah.

00:17:44.875 --> 00:17:48.083
I mean, they're basically idiots.
What do you want?

00:17:48.083 --> 00:17:51.458
But at least Hazama's got some brains.

00:17:51.458 --> 00:17:51.500
"<i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>" "Alexandre Dumas"
But at least Hazama's got some brains.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.250
"<i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>" "Alexandre Dumas"
You want to get back at Shiro, don't you?

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:54.625
You want to get back at Shiro, don't you?

00:17:54.625 --> 00:17:58.167
The famous novel of revenge:
<i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>.

00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:00.417
Seven volumes, 2,500 pages.

00:18:00.417 --> 00:18:03.542
Read this and feed the darkness within.

00:18:03.542 --> 00:18:05.750
He gives up on his revenge toward the end,

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:06.917
so don't bother reading that far.

00:18:06.917 --> 00:18:08.583
That's too hard!

00:18:08.583 --> 00:18:11.792
Hazama, your stuff is always
way too involved <i>and </i>way too dark!

00:18:11.792 --> 00:18:15.042
What? You've got to
cherish the darkness in your heart!

00:18:15.042 --> 00:18:18.250
Don't you have an easier way to cheer him up?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:21.000
This guy probably ain't the brightest--

00:18:22.292 --> 00:18:24.458
Uh-oh. He's getting all twitchy.

00:18:24.458 --> 00:18:27.500
Probably pissed that Terasaka called him dumb.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.417
No...

00:18:28.417 --> 00:18:32.292
It's the tentacles.
He's going to flip out on us again!

00:18:32.292 --> 00:18:35.375
I'm not like you, fine with any old way.

00:18:35.375 --> 00:18:38.750
I'll do it now! I'll kill him,
and victory will be mine!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.250
Terasaka!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:48.917
Hey, Itona. I thought about
killin' that octopus today, too.

00:18:48.917 --> 00:18:53.708
But you can't do it--not right away.

00:18:53.708 --> 00:18:58.000
Get rid of that impossible vision
of yours. It's easier that way.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.458
Shut up!

00:19:01.917 --> 00:19:05.750
That's the second time...
and you're weaker now. Easier to grab.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:09.500
Still hurts enough to wanna barf, though.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.833
And <i>that </i>just reminds me
of Muramatsu's ramen.

00:19:12.833 --> 00:19:13.500
Hey!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:13.708
"Intro to Business" "Restaurant Management Manual"
Hey!

00:19:13.708 --> 00:19:15.542
"Intro to Business" "Restaurant Management Manual"
That octopus told him to study business.

00:19:15.542 --> 00:19:18.292
"Ramen" "Gyoza" "Matsuraikan"
That octopus told him to study business.

00:19:18.292 --> 00:19:22.708
Gross ramen is fine for now.
One day, when he takes over,

00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:27.000
his new flavors and management skills
will get that joint jumpin'.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:32.542
He told Yoshida the same thing--
it could come in handy <i>someday</i>.

00:19:32.542 --> 00:19:34.667
C'mon, Itona.

00:19:34.667 --> 00:19:37.833
Don't let a couple losses throw you off course!

00:19:37.833 --> 00:19:40.375
All you gotta do is win <i>someday</i>.

00:19:40.375 --> 00:19:44.875
And when it comes to killin' that octopus...
it don't hafta be now.

00:19:44.875 --> 00:19:46.917
We can fail a hundred times over.

00:19:46.917 --> 00:19:52.125
Just kill him <i>once </i>before March... and we win.

00:19:52.125 --> 00:19:56.917
You can use the prize money
to buy back your dad's factory.

00:19:56.917 --> 00:19:59.583
Then your folks could come back.

00:19:59.583 --> 00:20:01.375
I can't stand this.

00:20:01.375 --> 00:20:05.917
What do I do until I come up with
my next vision of victory?

00:20:05.917 --> 00:20:07.000
Huh?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:13.125
You act like an idiot, like we did today!
That's what we're here for!

00:20:14.208 --> 00:20:18.292
What other idiot could say that
with a straight face?

00:20:18.292 --> 00:20:19.792
Although...

00:20:19.792 --> 00:20:24.542
Sometimes a word from an idiot
is all you need to chill things out.

00:20:25.458 --> 00:20:29.125
So I was being... hasty?

00:20:29.125 --> 00:20:30.250
Yeah.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.875
I think you were.

00:20:31.875 --> 00:20:35.792
That tint of attachment
is gone from your eyes, Itona.

00:20:35.792 --> 00:20:39.625
We can remove those
painful tentacle cells now.

00:20:39.625 --> 00:20:44.667
In losing one great power,
you gain many friends.

00:20:44.667 --> 00:20:46.375
You'll come kill me, won't you?

00:20:46.375 --> 00:20:46.583
"Yoshida Motors"
You'll come kill me, won't you?

00:20:46.583 --> 00:20:48.333
"Yoshida Motors"
Starting tomorrow?

00:20:48.333 --> 00:20:49.542
Starting tomorrow?

00:20:49.542 --> 00:20:51.208
Suit yourself.

00:20:51.208 --> 00:20:55.958
I'm sick of this power--
and this whole "brothers" thing, too.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:01.958
Hey, you made it! No more
busting through the wall, okay?

00:21:01.958 --> 00:21:05.083
'Morning! That bandana's a good look on you!

00:21:05.083 --> 00:21:08.500
Good morning. And how are you feeling?

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:12.292
Awful, now that I've lost my power.

00:21:12.292 --> 00:21:15.333
But I don't feel any weaker.

00:21:15.333 --> 00:21:19.417
In the end, I <i>will </i>kill you, Koro Sensei.

00:21:19.417 --> 00:21:21.542
And so problem child Itona Horibe

00:21:21.542 --> 00:21:24.000
finally joined our class.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:24.458
"Tentacle"
finally joined our class.

00:21:24.458 --> 00:21:26.792
"Tentacle"
Hey, Muramatsu--I'm broke.

00:21:26.792 --> 00:21:29.792
"Tentacle"
I'll try not to barf, so let me have some ramen.

00:21:29.792 --> 00:21:31.750
"Tentacle"
And he's in Terasaka's group.

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:47.750
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:53.125
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.125 --> 00:21:58.792
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:58.792 --> 00:22:03.958
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:03.958 --> 00:22:15.333
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.333 --> 00:22:20.917
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:20.917 --> 00:22:25.333
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.333 --> 00:22:32.167
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.167 --> 00:22:37.667
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.667 --> 00:22:43.167
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.167 --> 00:23:01.803
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
